  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="f47c5f76-3a56-5887-a7d1-a30fcbf3a90e" activityNameId="c548e457-736d-5207-ab5e-0d111dec4d9a" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Section bar extrusion, aluminium</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Section bar extrusion, aluminium
Heated aluminium is forced through one or more dies under extreme force to produce the desired shape. A great number of different shapes, and therefore possible apllications, can be achieved by extrusion of aluminium.;
Synonyms: profile extrusion; 
UUID: 4a0f787e-5316-36c2-9e11-188e470e6ca7
All the process steps, which can be attributed to semi-fabrication (sawing, scalping, preheating, extrusion, stretching, sawing, ageing and packaging), are included. Does not include the material beeing extruded, only the amount of scrap lost in waste is balanced as primary aluminium input. Includes the transport of the materials to the plant, but does not include the transport of the product to the customer.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Avarage technique for European Union. The infrastructure was assumed to be the same as for rolling steel.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature, estimation for transport and infrastructure 
Extrapolations: see technology and sampling procedure
Uncertainty adjustments: Precision of the data set is referred to be of 5 % by the reference, nevertheless uncertainty was estimated by filling out the uncertainty scoring
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_4a0f787e-5316-36c2-9e11-188e470e6ca7.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
